        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order identified; event review blocked by missing evidence\n\nThe September manufacturing order ending in **1070** is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for the **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot determine without the event details |\n\nThe supplied timestamp has **no timezone specified**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that newly created transactions falling in or before a period in **Pending Close** are not staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\n*Source: “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233, printed page 225.*\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe accessible task records contain the work order, cost period, and policy excerpt, but **no cost-event rows**. Access to the supporting event records was denied. I requested authorized event evidence, but none was received.\n\nAccordingly, **I cannot confirm or rule out a post–Pending Close event**, identify its source transaction or amount, or judge its recorded status. The review remains incomplete rather than treating missing evidence as proof that no late event occurred.\n\nNo database records were changed. The audit findings and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_feb3129efbb3/audit-report.json`.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
